1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,870
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,170
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,810 --> 00:00:05,980
(Episode 30)

4
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:08,310
Why? Why can't I do that?

5
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:12,380
Girl, do I really have to
spell it out for you?

6
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:16,220
Maybe when you were young
and foolish, sure,

7
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:19,720
but if you appreciate how my sister
took you in and raised you,

8
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:22,060
you should behave yourself by now.

9
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:24,230
Stop upsetting my sister.

10
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:27,100
Aunt Ri Ja.

11
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:28,770
What? What is it?

12
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,300
Can't you keep your mouth shut?

13
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:44,550
- Da Mi.
- I'm fine, Mom.

14
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:47,090
Please just take her outside.

15
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:51,320
Go downstairs right now.

16
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:53,660
But, Mi Mi,

17
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:58,030
no matter how nicely
I try to talk to Da Mi,

18
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:00,130
she just keeps pouting.

19
00:01:00,870 --> 00:01:02,170
I told you to go downstairs.

20
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:18,950
Mom, I asked you to leave too.

21
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:23,890
I'm so sorry, sweetie.

22
00:01:25,290 --> 00:01:27,660
You shouldn't have to hear
such hurtful things.

23
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:32,360
You know how your aunt is.
She has no filter.

24
00:01:33,330 --> 00:01:34,900
I'll go downstairs
and give her a stern talking-to...

25
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,970
so this never happens again, okay?

26
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:40,740
Just for today,

27
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:44,140
please let it go in one ear
and out the other.

28
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,080
Mom,

29
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:48,750
can you really do that?

30
00:01:51,050 --> 00:01:52,050
Do what?

31
00:01:53,150 --> 00:01:55,620
No matter how sharp
and piercing the words are,

32
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:59,060
can you really just let them go
in one ear and out the other?

33
00:02:00,730 --> 00:02:03,190
As time passes and you get older,

34
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,200
does that actually become possible?

35
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:09,100
Because for me, Mom,

36
00:02:10,270 --> 00:02:12,140
no matter how hard I try,
I just can't do it.

37
00:02:16,110 --> 00:02:18,240
I'll head downstairs
and come back up in a bit.

38
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:19,810
Get some rest by yourself.

39
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,890
Sweetheart, Da Mi.

40
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:30,820
Yes?

41
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:33,120
Even at my age,

42
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:35,630
truth be told,
I can't really do it either.

43
00:02:56,610 --> 00:02:58,150
Maybe when you were young
and foolish, sure,

44
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:01,120
but if you appreciate how my sister
took you in and raised you...

45
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:03,190
If you appreciate how she
took you in and raised you...

46
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:05,420
If you appreciate how she
took you in and raised you...

47
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:35,250
Hey, stop crying.

48
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:37,620
I came down, so it's fine now.

49
00:03:38,590 --> 00:03:39,590
Okay.

50
00:03:40,630 --> 00:03:43,230
I'll give you a good job sticker.

51
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:45,960
What?

52
00:03:52,370 --> 00:03:55,010
In one ear and out the other. Right.

53
00:03:56,010 --> 00:03:57,380
Let it go this time too.

54
00:03:59,010 --> 00:04:00,610
Even Mom said it's hard to do.

55
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,890
Kang Su Ah, you're home early.

56
00:04:14,190 --> 00:04:16,290
Yes. Uncle Dae Chi,
what did you buy?

57
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,700
Ramyeon and drinks.

58
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:20,800
Do you want a drink, Su Ah?

59
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:22,730
Here.

60
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:32,980
Dad, Uncle Dae Chi gave it to me.

61
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,310
You'll get cavities, so no.

62
00:04:35,110 --> 00:04:36,650
Then is it okay
for you to get cavities?

63
00:04:38,050 --> 00:04:39,450
Sorry, sweetie.

64
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,350
Right now, your dad...

65
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:45,490
is boiling mad on the inside
because of your uncle.

66
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:48,430
- What did I do?
- Hey, Kang Dae Chi.

67
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:50,560
Upstairs on the second floor,

68
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:54,370
there was total chaos
because of you, you punk.

69
00:04:54,370 --> 00:04:55,430
Because of me?

70
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:57,640
What are you talking about?

71
00:04:58,070 --> 00:04:59,840
- Make some sense.
- Hey.

72
00:05:00,070 --> 00:05:02,810
You're 1,130,000 dollars in debt,

73
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:05,380
yet you turn our house
into a total disaster.

74
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:07,780
I see you got money from Mom...

75
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:10,450
and happily went skipping off
to the convenience store.

76
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:14,150
Without even caring
where that money came from,

77
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:15,220
you selfish jerk.

78
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:20,120
Sure, as long as you survive,
who cares about anyone else?

79
00:05:20,630 --> 00:05:22,090
First Kkangda earlier, and now you.

80
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:25,660
Is getting 80,000 dollars from Mom
really something to be cursed out for?

81
00:05:26,030 --> 00:05:29,370
And where on earth
did that money come from...

82
00:05:29,470 --> 00:05:31,300
for you to jump down
my throat like this?

83
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:32,540
Darn it.

84
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:36,340
I'm letting you off only because
you owe 1,130,000 dollars.

85
00:05:37,810 --> 00:05:39,680
Sweetie, let's go
change your clothes.

86
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:41,310
We need to go see a movie.

87
00:05:41,810 --> 00:05:42,810
Okay.

88
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:47,690
Throw it out.

89
00:05:50,990 --> 00:05:51,990
Unbelievable.

90
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:02,370
I said I was sorry.

91
00:06:03,170 --> 00:06:05,700
I really mean it.

92
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:11,880
Aren't you opening for dinner?

93
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:16,180
Mrs. Choi has been
all alone at the restaurant.

94
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:18,580
Ri Ja.

95
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:20,990
Yes?

96
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,720
Jo Ri Ja.

97
00:06:24,020 --> 00:06:26,620
Tell me. I'm listening.

98
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:28,630
Pack your bags.

99
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:32,460
What?

100
00:06:33,130 --> 00:06:34,870
Get out of my house.

101
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:39,100
Mi Mi. Are you done talking?

102
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:40,170
Do you mean that?

103
00:06:40,910 --> 00:06:43,010
Anyone who makes my child cry,

104
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:46,810
I'll never forgive them,
even if it's you.

105
00:06:49,710 --> 00:06:50,720
How much...

106
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:54,120
have you been hurting Da Mi
behind my back all this time?

107
00:06:54,590 --> 00:06:56,590
How could my one and only sister...

108
00:06:56,690 --> 00:06:58,690
Don't you know what she means to me?

109
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,120
Don't you know she is my daughter?

110
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:02,590
This is ridiculous.

111
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:05,760
Look who's talking.

112
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,730
How could my one and only sister...

113
00:07:09,870 --> 00:07:13,340
Do you really have no idea
why I treated Da Mi like that...

114
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:16,310
or why I had no choice
but to act that way?

115
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,780
Are you saying you did it for me?

116
00:07:21,250 --> 00:07:22,280
Then...

117
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:24,180
did I do it for myself?

118
00:07:24,450 --> 00:07:26,350
When your husband...

119
00:07:26,550 --> 00:07:28,520
cheated on you
with the waitress you hired...

120
00:07:28,590 --> 00:07:30,190
and walked out of this house,

121
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,520
you brought Da Mi here
and raised her.

122
00:07:32,790 --> 00:07:33,790
From that day until now,

123
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:35,490
I haven't stopped worrying
about you for even a single day.

124
00:07:35,730 --> 00:07:39,160
I felt so bad seeing you suffer
when you didn't have to.

125
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:41,730
So in my own way,
I tried to shield you.

126
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:44,870
I'm raising my own child.
Why would you feel bad for me?

127
00:07:44,870 --> 00:07:47,340
Did you give birth to her? No.

128
00:07:47,410 --> 00:07:49,210
Neither did your husband.

129
00:07:49,270 --> 00:07:50,740
You don't know whose child she is,

130
00:07:50,810 --> 00:07:52,480
and you picked her up
off the street.

131
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:54,810
After raising her well
all this time,

132
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:56,980
shouldn't you get to lean
on her a little now?

133
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:04,520
Get out.

134
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,390
Didn't you hear me? Get out.

135
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,660
Fine, I'm leaving.

136
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:46,500
Was it wrong of me
to take that money from Mom?

137
00:08:47,530 --> 00:08:49,400
Why did this blow back on Da Mi?

138
00:09:02,680 --> 00:09:06,020
When will I ever save up enough
to go there now?

139
00:09:07,790 --> 00:09:09,290
I really wanted to go.

140
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:11,820
I really thought I would.

141
00:09:14,630 --> 00:09:15,630
Aunt Da Mi.

142
00:09:21,470 --> 00:09:23,130
Hey, Su Ah.

143
00:09:23,670 --> 00:09:25,000
Where did you find that teddy bear?

144
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:30,580
When Dad and I played hide-and-seek,
I hid under your desk.

145
00:09:30,910 --> 00:09:33,040
It was inside a black plastic bag.

146
00:09:33,950 --> 00:09:36,810
Can I hold this
and take it to the library?

147
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:39,780
Did I leave it there?

148
00:09:41,550 --> 00:09:44,290
Sure, you can,
but you can't lose it.

149
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:47,390
- Why?
- It might be old,

150
00:09:48,260 --> 00:09:50,800
but this is a gift
I got from a certain man.

151
00:09:51,330 --> 00:09:52,500
That's right.

152
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:55,970
Mom told me all gifts are special,
no matter how big or small they are.

153
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:57,300
Right?

154
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:00,440
Right. Are you going with your dad?

155
00:10:00,710 --> 00:10:03,310
Su Ah, there you are.

156
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:08,280
I told you to put
that grubby bear away.

157
00:10:08,450 --> 00:10:09,480
You never listen.

158
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:12,150
- Let's go.
- Okay, Dad.

159
00:10:16,350 --> 00:10:17,360
Hey, Da Mi.

160
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:20,760
- Yes?
- Man, Aunt Ri Ja...

161
00:10:21,190 --> 00:10:24,000
has no filter whatsoever.

162
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,200
When will she ever grow up?

163
00:10:37,110 --> 00:10:38,280
Can you move your hand away?

164
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:40,710
Should I?

165
00:10:41,210 --> 00:10:42,310
I was just about to.

166
00:10:43,510 --> 00:10:44,720
Let's go to the movies, sweetie.

167
00:10:45,650 --> 00:10:49,750
Dad, filters are for water.
They make water clear.

168
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:55,030
What?
That's not what I meant, sweetie.

169
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,200
Let's just get going, okay?

170
00:10:59,030 --> 00:11:00,030
Bye.

171
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,730
You really take after your mom.

172
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:17,750
Danny, I'm looking
at the contract now.

173
00:11:18,650 --> 00:11:23,020
If our investment goes as planned,
we can secure a six percent stake.

174
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:26,020
No, that's not enough.

175
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:28,860
Let's try to push it
to eight percent.

176
00:11:29,330 --> 00:11:30,390
They'll think we're suckers.

177
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:35,170
We agreed we'd act like
we'd give them everything.

178
00:11:35,170 --> 00:11:36,200
What's wrong?

179
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:38,470
- Okay, Boss.
- Good.

180
00:11:41,210 --> 00:11:42,940
How did your Korean get so good?

181
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,080
Yes?

182
00:11:47,850 --> 00:11:50,110
- Uncle In Sung.
- Looks like you're busy.

183
00:11:50,650 --> 00:11:52,150
A little.

184
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:53,950
Sorry about this.
It's quite a mess, isn't it?

185
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:55,250
It's all right.

186
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:57,660
I was just stopping by
to see your face for a bit.

187
00:12:00,090 --> 00:12:03,460
Do Yun is at a vendor meeting
with Assistant Manager Kang, dear.

188
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:05,560
That's too bad.

189
00:12:06,130 --> 00:12:07,160
Since I took the time to come out,

190
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:09,470
I wanted to take everyone out
and buy dinner.

191
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:11,370
Well, there's always another day.

192
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:14,310
Seung Yun.
It looks like you'll need...

193
00:12:14,310 --> 00:12:16,640
two or three assistants
in your office.

194
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:19,910
The company will support you,
so why not hire them quickly?

195
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:21,710
No, that's all right.
You already gave me...

196
00:12:21,710 --> 00:12:23,180
a generous signing bonus.

197
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:25,120
It makes sense for me
to build my own team.

198
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:26,750
That's how I worked in the US too.

199
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:28,720
Are you looking into it?

200
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:30,220
Oh, yes.

201
00:12:30,290 --> 00:12:32,620
There actually happens to be someone
I want to work with.

202
00:12:32,690 --> 00:12:35,130
- I've already made an offer.
- Really?

203
00:12:35,330 --> 00:12:37,600
And they haven't decided yet?

204
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:40,630
Right, they probably need time
to think it over.

205
00:12:42,170 --> 00:12:44,600
Jaden Cha offered to work together,

206
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:47,040
and they said they needed time
to think about it?

207
00:12:48,370 --> 00:12:49,770
Who on earth could that be?

208
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:53,080
Right? Now I'm curious too.

209
00:12:54,910 --> 00:12:57,210
You'll meet them soon,
if it's meant to be.

210
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,820
Meant to be?

211
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:02,420
Leave it to an artist...

212
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:05,020
to use such sentimental words,
our Seung Yun.

213
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:07,460
Do I? Am I sentimental?

214
00:13:12,430 --> 00:13:13,430
Yes.

215
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,600
Director Ju.

216
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:24,480
Would it be all right
if I left a bit early today?

217
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:27,710
Aren't you feeling well?

218
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:30,650
Pardon? Well...

219
00:13:31,550 --> 00:13:34,390
My stomach is acting up again...

220
00:13:35,650 --> 00:13:36,990
I'm so sorry to keep doing this.

221
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:40,560
It's all right.
You didn't choose to be sick.

222
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,760
Go on ahead and head home.

223
00:13:43,090 --> 00:13:44,660
- Thank you.
- Of course.

224
00:13:44,730 --> 00:13:46,830
(Director Ju Kyung Ho)

225
00:13:49,270 --> 00:13:50,730
(Madam Chairwoman)

226
00:13:55,010 --> 00:13:56,010
Yes, Madam Chairwoman.

227
00:13:56,170 --> 00:13:59,010
I'm sorry to disturb you
during consultation hours.

228
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:00,780
Not at all. Please, go ahead.

229
00:14:01,250 --> 00:14:04,950
I've been thinking it over
carefully.

230
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:08,250
If a person's past
is excessively clean,

231
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:10,350
what do you think
about flipping the script...

232
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:12,890
and looking at it
from another angle?

233
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:15,590
Madam Chairwoman, do you mean...

234
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:19,560
The person might have
deliberately erased it.

235
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:21,000
Otherwise, it makes no sense.

236
00:14:21,370 --> 00:14:24,740
Yes, leaving no trace at all
really doesn't add up.

237
00:14:25,370 --> 00:14:27,870
Look into it.

238
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:29,740
Understood.

239
00:14:40,350 --> 00:14:41,350
(Trends Change Quickly,)

240
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:42,590
(But Trust Is Not Built That Way)

241
00:14:52,130 --> 00:14:54,130
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

242
00:15:03,670 --> 00:15:05,680
Aren't you going to open for dinner?

243
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,350
Customers will be rushing in soon.

244
00:15:08,410 --> 00:15:10,610
Why hasn't Mi Mi come out yet?

245
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:13,580
Well...

246
00:15:14,150 --> 00:15:15,290
Mrs. Choi.

247
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:19,620
Could I talk to you for a moment?

248
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,030
Talk?

249
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:24,830
Yes, just for a moment.

250
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:30,100
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

251
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:38,840
Are you asking for a raise?

252
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:41,380
No.

253
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:43,210
Then what?

254
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:49,920
You've been managing my salary
all this time, Mrs. Choi.

255
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:51,020
And?

256
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:55,030
Because you kept getting
ripped off by men.

257
00:15:55,430 --> 00:15:57,030
When Mi Mi and I bailed you out...

258
00:15:57,030 --> 00:16:00,560
of the police station
for the last time,

259
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,370
that was the condition
for you to live in our house.

260
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:08,610
You don't need to bring up
my dark past.

261
00:16:09,570 --> 00:16:10,570
Well...

262
00:16:10,910 --> 00:16:13,840
how much money
have I saved up so far?

263
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:15,550
Please let me know.

264
00:16:15,810 --> 00:16:17,580
Why do you want to know?

265
00:16:20,950 --> 00:16:24,920
I think I should move out
of this house.

266
00:16:25,490 --> 00:16:27,460
I think I need to live on my own.

267
00:16:28,130 --> 00:16:30,130
How much do I have?

268
00:16:30,430 --> 00:16:33,260
Do I have enough
for a tiny studio apartment?

269
00:16:34,230 --> 00:16:37,630
Well, I scattered it
all over the place,

270
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,200
so I'm not really sure.

271
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:42,440
What do you mean by that, Mrs. Choi?

272
00:16:43,310 --> 00:16:46,840
Where on earth
did you scatter my money,

273
00:16:46,910 --> 00:16:49,480
money I've never even laid eyes on?

274
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,850
Well, it's been so long.

275
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:53,750
Where did I put it?

276
00:16:54,950 --> 00:16:56,620
I'll have to look for it.

277
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:59,620
Who knows? It might have
just flown away...

278
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:01,430
when I wasn't looking.

279
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:04,960
Mrs. Choi.

280
00:17:27,790 --> 00:17:30,650
Where did Mom go?
Did she go to the restaurant?

281
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,060
(Da Mi's Wedding Fund)

282
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:44,230
(Da Mi's Wedding Fund)

283
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,910
This is driving me crazy.

284
00:17:51,010 --> 00:17:54,140
(Regular Deposit: 200 Dollars
Additional Deposit: 150 Dollars)

285
00:17:54,210 --> 00:17:56,450
(Da Mi's Wedding Fund)

286
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:03,990
(Consultation Room)

287
00:18:03,990 --> 00:18:05,660
- Have a seat.
- Okay.

288
00:18:13,430 --> 00:18:16,930
You don't look very well.
What seems to be the problem?

289
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:21,540
My stomach has felt so heavy
for a few days now.

290
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:25,940
I was going to tough it out
because it felt bearable,

291
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:27,440
but I thought it would be better...

292
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:29,550
to get checked
before dinner service.

293
00:18:30,710 --> 00:18:33,380
Do you usually have
digestive issues?

294
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:36,850
No, I usually have a strong stomach.

295
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:41,390
I think it might be from the stress
of family matters lately.

296
00:18:42,190 --> 00:18:43,190
Dr. Ju,

297
00:18:43,530 --> 00:18:45,000
could you prescribe
some effective medicine...

298
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:47,530
to relieve this tightness
in my stomach?

299
00:18:49,130 --> 00:18:52,140
At this rate, I won't even
be able to run my restaurant.

300
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:55,910
I can prescribe you some medication,

301
00:18:57,140 --> 00:19:00,110
but are you having
any other symptoms?

302
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:02,350
Other symptoms?

303
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:06,320
Have you noticed any significant
weight loss recently?

304
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:10,620
I'm not sure.
I don't really weigh myself.

305
00:19:12,190 --> 00:19:15,160
I'm always too busy
just trying to get by.

306
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:23,530
(Debtor Summary, Name: Kang Dae Chi)

307
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:32,710
Cha Se Na.

308
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:34,950
Your brother comes home,
and you don't even greet him?

309
00:19:35,810 --> 00:19:38,020
You're back? Where's Seung Yun?

310
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:41,420
He's holed up at the office
and won't budge.

311
00:19:42,490 --> 00:19:44,120
He didn't make it
in the States for nothing.

312
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:47,420
By the way,

313
00:19:47,890 --> 00:19:49,360
what are you looking at so intently?

314
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:54,500
Kang Dae Chi?

315
00:19:55,470 --> 00:19:56,530
What kind of name is that?

316
00:19:57,330 --> 00:19:58,500
Was he born in Daechi-dong?

317
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:00,800
Maybe?

318
00:20:01,270 --> 00:20:02,840
I'll ask him
when I see him tomorrow morning.

319
00:20:04,110 --> 00:20:05,840
He's pretty good-looking,
right, Do Yun?

320
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:09,010
Even if he is,

321
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:10,850
what are you going to do
with a debtor?

322
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:13,950
Can't I even say
a handsome guy is handsome?

323
00:20:14,990 --> 00:20:15,990
Hey, Do Yun,

324
00:20:16,350 --> 00:20:18,420
what does a manager
at a major company have to do...

325
00:20:18,490 --> 00:20:19,720
to get suspended from his job?

326
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:21,430
Suspended?

327
00:20:22,030 --> 00:20:23,460
Well, usually...

328
00:20:23,530 --> 00:20:25,500
for causing massive damage
or financial loss to the company.

329
00:20:26,100 --> 00:20:29,100
Breach of trust, embezzlement,
leaking confidential company data,

330
00:20:29,170 --> 00:20:30,730
or being involved
in a criminal case.

331
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,240
Why do you ask?

332
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:35,970
So it means he committed a crime,
either way.

333
00:20:41,010 --> 00:20:43,250
See? That's why I told you
not to work at that clinic.

334
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:46,280
Do you know how shocked I was
when I went there today...

335
00:20:46,350 --> 00:20:47,880
to get you to quit?

336
00:20:48,250 --> 00:20:52,920
I never imagined
I'd run into her this soon.

337
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,790
Do you have any idea how careful
I've been about hiding from her?

338
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:59,630
I never thought that old woman
would barge into the clinic.

339
00:21:00,830 --> 00:21:02,900
Are you going to keep calling her
"that old woman"?

340
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:06,000
Do you think you'll never get old?
Honestly, what's with you...

341
00:21:06,270 --> 00:21:07,440
I can't help hating her.

342
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:09,140
What do you expect after all
the grief she gave me?

343
00:21:10,370 --> 00:21:12,010
So are you still going to
keep working there?

344
00:21:12,110 --> 00:21:13,580
Fine, I'll quit.

345
00:21:13,710 --> 00:21:15,780
I don't want to die young
of a heart attack either.

346
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:16,950
I'll quit, okay?

347
00:21:23,850 --> 00:21:24,890
Don't tell me it's her again.

348
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:27,290
Darn it.

349
00:21:27,990 --> 00:21:29,690
What are you going to do?

350
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:33,800
Knowing my mom,
if we don't open this door,

351
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,800
she'll call someone
to tear it right off its hinges.

352
00:21:35,870 --> 00:21:36,870
Don't you know her by now?

353
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:40,240
I can't take this anymore,
seriously.

354
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:51,380
You're here?

355
00:21:54,620 --> 00:21:56,990
I heard you saw her at the clinic.

356
00:21:57,490 --> 00:21:59,820
She told me. I saw you too,

357
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:01,660
earlier this afternoon.

358
00:22:04,730 --> 00:22:08,230
Please, have a seat right here.
Here.

359
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,330
I don't plan to talk long,

360
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:13,100
and you're not worth it anyway.

361
00:22:13,870 --> 00:22:15,040
Just listen.

362
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:19,080
I disowned you with my own hands,

363
00:22:19,810 --> 00:22:22,380
saying you were no longer my son,

364
00:22:23,150 --> 00:22:24,350
and cut ties with you.

365
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:27,380
Seeing how low you've fallen
these past few days...

366
00:22:27,450 --> 00:22:29,420
was so appalling...

367
00:22:29,750 --> 00:22:32,420
that I must have lost my mind
coming by, but...

368
00:22:33,860 --> 00:22:34,860
Mom.

369
00:22:35,260 --> 00:22:37,030
Who's your mother?

370
00:22:37,930 --> 00:22:41,160
Neither of you even deserves
to be called human.

371
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:43,830
Never show your face to me again.

372
00:22:44,430 --> 00:22:46,670
And especially not
in front of Mi Mi!

373
00:22:47,570 --> 00:22:51,840
If you do, that very day,
I'll kill both of you with my bare...

374
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:53,810
Who...

375
00:22:55,050 --> 00:22:56,210
Mom, I'm home.

376
00:22:57,380 --> 00:22:58,380
Ye Ri.

377
00:22:59,080 --> 00:23:00,220
Who are you?

378
00:23:04,350 --> 00:23:06,220
Mom, who is she?

379
00:23:06,860 --> 00:23:08,020
Well, you see...

380
00:23:08,790 --> 00:23:10,460
Well, Ye Ri, she's...

381
00:23:10,530 --> 00:23:11,900
- Say hello, sweetheart.
- You see...

382
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:13,600
Remember I mentioned her?

383
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:17,600
- She's our landlady.
- Landlady?

384
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,340
Landlady?

385
00:23:21,470 --> 00:23:22,740
This is our daughter.

386
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:26,080
She works at that famous company,
Hwanggeum Apparel,

387
00:23:26,140 --> 00:23:28,250
and has a very promising career.

388
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:31,820
Hello, I'm Kang Ye Ri.

389
00:23:32,580 --> 00:23:34,250
May I ask what brings you
to our place?

390
00:23:36,390 --> 00:23:37,520
Well, you know,

391
00:23:37,650 --> 00:23:40,690
she got noise complaints
from our neighbors,

392
00:23:40,790 --> 00:23:43,960
so she came to ask us
to keep it down.

393
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:45,260
Right?

394
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:49,670
Wait, we live in a semi-basement.
What noise complaint could there be?

395
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:07,980
Mom is at the restaurant, right?

396
00:24:09,150 --> 00:24:11,790
Yes. She's handling the dinner rush.

397
00:24:12,460 --> 00:24:13,820
Come sit down for a second.

398
00:24:22,300 --> 00:24:25,000
Aunt Ri Ja, about earlier, I...

399
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:26,770
Your mother...

400
00:24:27,840 --> 00:24:30,640
My sister ended up going
to the clinic, it seems.

401
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:34,610
Her kids have caused her
so much heartache lately.

402
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:36,050
What's wrong with her?
Is it serious?

403
00:24:36,310 --> 00:24:38,820
She took some medicine
and went back to work.

404
00:24:42,150 --> 00:24:43,150
Listen.

405
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:49,130
I think it'd be best
if you moved out.

406
00:24:51,830 --> 00:24:54,400
- What?
- I'm sick and tired of this mess,

407
00:24:54,730 --> 00:24:57,030
so I was going to move out
of this house myself.

408
00:24:57,670 --> 00:24:59,640
I asked Mrs. Choi
how much I've saved up...

409
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:01,140
from my wages all this time,

410
00:25:02,140 --> 00:25:03,710
but she said she scattered it
here and there...

411
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:05,280
and can't even remember.

412
00:25:06,310 --> 00:25:09,510
You must have saved up
a decent amount of money by now.

413
00:25:10,350 --> 00:25:13,080
If you and I keep clashing
like this under the same roof,

414
00:25:13,550 --> 00:25:15,290
my sister will be caught
in the middle...

415
00:25:15,390 --> 00:25:16,590
and get hurt every single time.

416
00:25:17,550 --> 00:25:19,060
Honestly, you don't want
that either, do you?

417
00:25:19,860 --> 00:25:23,230
Do you really hate me that much?

418
00:25:25,230 --> 00:25:26,560
Did I say I hate you?

419
00:25:27,560 --> 00:25:29,070
Whenever I see
how hard my sister's life is,

420
00:25:29,170 --> 00:25:30,170
and then I look at you,

421
00:25:30,230 --> 00:25:34,740
I just get this sick, bitter feeling
churning inside me.

422
00:25:35,840 --> 00:25:37,210
Is Mom's hardship...

423
00:25:38,070 --> 00:25:39,410
all my fault?

424
00:25:40,810 --> 00:25:41,910
To be honest,

425
00:25:43,210 --> 00:25:46,150
at some point,
that's what I started to believe.

426
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:47,480
Since when?

427
00:25:49,050 --> 00:25:50,050
Since you...

428
00:25:50,990 --> 00:25:53,620
walked into this house
and started living here.

429
00:25:55,190 --> 00:25:56,190
Why?

430
00:25:56,760 --> 00:25:59,900
Do I really have to spell it out
for you to understand?

431
00:26:02,300 --> 00:26:05,800
Yes, ever since you came
into this house,

432
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:08,540
my sister's life
got completely messed up.

433
00:26:09,010 --> 00:26:10,640
My brother-in-law cheated on her...

434
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:12,080
with another woman,
had a child with her,

435
00:26:12,410 --> 00:26:14,480
and ran off to start a new family.
Am I wrong?

436
00:26:15,550 --> 00:26:19,050
Auntie, how can you blame me
for that, too?

437
00:26:19,980 --> 00:26:23,090
Hey, what can I do when I see you
and can't help thinking that way?

438
00:26:23,450 --> 00:26:24,990
I didn't want to say it.

439
00:26:25,160 --> 00:26:27,590
You knew how I felt,
yet you kept pushing me.

440
00:26:28,860 --> 00:26:29,860
Seriously...

441
00:26:44,510 --> 00:26:46,240
Ever since you came into this house,

442
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:49,010
my sister's life
got completely messed up.

443
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:07,100
Yes, this is Manager Kang Da Mi...

444
00:27:08,230 --> 00:27:09,300
This is Kang Da Mi.

445
00:27:11,070 --> 00:27:12,140
Yes, go ahead.

446
00:27:13,870 --> 00:27:16,610
I'll take the job.

447
00:27:20,080 --> 00:27:21,610
I was actually waiting
for your call,

448
00:27:21,610 --> 00:27:23,950
so this is truly wonderful news
to hear, Kang Da Mi.

449
00:27:25,020 --> 00:27:26,680
When can you start?

450
00:27:27,580 --> 00:27:29,520
I'd like to start tomorrow,
if possible.

451
00:27:30,250 --> 00:27:31,550
Sounds good.

452
00:27:32,690 --> 00:27:34,160
Let's start working together
tomorrow, then.

453
00:27:35,230 --> 00:27:36,230
Goodbye.

454
00:27:57,050 --> 00:27:58,880
(Mission: Mompossible)

455
00:28:14,930 --> 00:28:17,430
Are you properly managing
the money you made...

456
00:28:17,500 --> 00:28:18,970
working as a designer in the States?

457
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,540
Seung Yun, how much
did you actually save up?

458
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:23,670
What savings?
I spent it all having fun. Why?

459
00:28:23,740 --> 00:28:26,280
That woman is actually
coming to work at the company now.

460
00:28:26,340 --> 00:28:28,750
What are you talking about?
That woman is coming to the company?

461
00:28:30,050 --> 00:28:32,020
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
